The DC directory contains procedures to load a design, compile, elaborate it and check the consistency of delivered CTL model
 against Synopsys Design Compiler.
The script DC_integrity_check_with_ctl_template.tcl is a template script that can be customized to suite the design and
relies on RDF settings.
The intent is to use it in a similar fashion as setup_project_tamplate.csh and project_template prior any customization. 
In order to run the script do the following steps:

-  Make sure that setup_project.csh and project.tcl are properly set.

-  It works only with KEEP_PATHS set to 0 and only with absolute paths

-  Copy template script to the working script:
   cp DC_integrity_check_with_ctl_template.tcl DC_integrity_check_with_ctl.tcl
   
-  Customize DC_integrity_check_with_ctl.tcl following the varaibles that need to be set. Also refer to the RDF user guide
   and mind that the script name 'DC_integrity_check_with_ctl.tcl' is mandatory within this flow.

-  Load the required Synopys DC compiler:
   module load synopsys/2014.09-SP3

- The script must be run within DC directory by:
  source ./run_DC

- Alternatively, the DCShell can be also run interactively. To do so use the following 
     '$LSF dc_shell-t -output_log_file dc.log'  

Note: this is a reference flow only -no synthesis nor DFT insertion is performed and only one standard 
  cell library mihgt be referenced (if referenced).  It is expected that customer synthesis will leverage multiple libraries and 
  VT levels as well as a customer-preferred test insertion flow.

